                  overrideAPIName="false">
            <parameterSet xmlns="http://schemas.active-endpoints.com/appmodules/screenflow/2021/04/taskflowModel.xsd">
               <parameter name="XRefCode" direction="in" type="string" description="Dayforce employee XRefCode"/>
               <parameter name="NewPersonVinciId" direction="in" type="string" description="VINCI ID returned by CreatePersonAndContract_Process"/>
               <parameter name="access_token" direction="in" type="string" description="Dayforce bearer token"/>
            </parameterSet>
            <appliesTo/>
            <description>Scenario 4 (VINCI ID Writeback), Create path only. Wraps Dayforce API 3.1.4 (Write VINCI ID Back, PATCH EmployeeProperties). Invoked by the Orchestrator immediately after CreatePersonAndContract_Process succeeds (build guide 4.10, 4.15 step 4).</description>
            <tags/>
            <generator>Informatica Process Designer 11</generator>
            <notes>Hand-authored against the CPD-Dayforce Functional Design &amp; API Build Guide v1.0 - see README_IICS_BUILD_NOTES.md for schema caveats. OPEN ITEM (from the design doc, section 3.1.4 / 4.1): the Dayforce EmployeeProperties XRefCode that identifies the "VINCI ID" custom property is still pending client confirmation; the WriteVinciIdToDayforce connector action carries a literal &lt;VINCI_ID_PROPERTY_XREFCODE_TBD&gt; placeholder in its request body that must be replaced before this process can run successfully.</notes>
            <deployment skipIfRunning="false" suspendOnFault="false" tracingLevel="none">
               <rest/>
            </deployment>
            <extData>
               <nvpair name="treatEmptyStringAsNotNull">false</nvpair>
               <nvpair name="treatEmptyObjectListAsArray">true</nvpair>
            </extData>
            <flow id="f6-writeback">
